<title>SOUTH AFRICA: RUGBY UNION-NATAL WIN SECOND SUCCESSIVE CURRIE CUP.</title>
<headline>RUGBY UNION-NATAL WIN SECOND SUCCESSIVE CURRIE CUP.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-10-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Defending champions Natal</p>
<p>won South Africa's domestic Currie Cup competition for the</p>
<p>second successive year after beating Transvaal 33-15 (halftime</p>
<p>10-9) at Ellis Park on Saturday.</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Natal - Tries: Jeremy Thomson, Andre Joubert (2).</p>
<p>Conversions: Henry Honiball (3). Penalties: Honiball (4).</p>
<p>Transvaal - Penalties: Gavin Lawless (5).</p>
</text>
